1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,420
On 18 October 1965,
a helicopter disappears over the

2
00:00:04,420 --> 00:00:06,610
jungle of Vietnam.

3
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:09,010
On board is a captain
of the American

4
00:00:09,010 --> 00:00:11,870
Special Forces: Larry Thorne.

5
00:00:11,890 --> 00:00:15,790
Only 34 years later is
the crash site found.

6
00:00:15,810 --> 00:00:17,270
Yet this man wore three

7
00:00:17,270 --> 00:00:19,180
different uniforms in his life.

8
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:21,790
He fought for Finland
against the Soviet Union,

9
00:00:21,790 --> 00:00:24,480
he served in the Waffen-SS,

10
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:27,990
and he died as an
officer of the US Army.

11
00:00:28,010 --> 00:00:30,230
In his homeland he was known

12
00:00:30,230 --> 00:00:33,390
by another name: Lauri Törni.

13
00:00:33,420 --> 00:00:40,190
Lauri Allan Törni was born on 28
May 1919 in Viipuri, a port city

14
00:00:40,190 --> 00:00:42,050
in Karelia.

15
00:00:42,050 --> 00:00:43,940
At the time it
belonged to Finland;

16
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:47,720
today it is called Vyborg
and lies in Russia.

17
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:51,310
In 1938 he was called
up for military service.

18
00:00:51,310 --> 00:00:55,460
A year later,
in November 1939, the Soviet

19
00:00:55,460 --> 00:00:58,000
Union attacked Finland.

20
00:00:58,030 --> 00:01:01,970
In the Winter War,
Törni fought north of Lake Ladoga,

21
00:01:01,970 --> 00:01:05,680
where Finnish units destroyed
encircled Soviet troops

22
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:07,010
near Lemetti.

23
00:01:07,030 --> 00:01:10,730
When the war ended
in March 1940,

24
00:01:10,730 --> 00:01:12,790
he was a reserve lieutenant.

25
00:01:12,810 --> 00:01:15,710
Finland had to give up
large parts of Karelia,

26
00:01:15,710 --> 00:01:18,950
including his
hometown of Viipuri.

27
00:01:18,970 --> 00:01:21,880
Finland now sought
support from Germany.

28
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:27,200
In June 1941, Törni travelled to
Vienna and completed several weeks

29
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:30,460
of training with
the Waffen-SS there.

30
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:33,630
That same summer he returned
to Finland, because the

31
00:01:33,630 --> 00:01:36,130
Continuation War
was beginning there.

32
00:01:36,150 --> 00:01:41,640
In 1943 he was given command of
a small unit that was soon simply

33
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:44,000
called Detachment Törni.

34
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,940
His men operated far
behind Soviet lines,

35
00:01:47,940 --> 00:01:51,860
laid ambushes and often
returned only after days.

36
00:01:51,890 --> 00:01:55,480
According to reports,
the Soviet side put a bounty of

37
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:58,490
three million
Finnish marks on him.

38
00:01:58,510 --> 00:02:03,160
In the summer of 1944 he fought
at Ilomantsi, in one of the

39
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:06,040
last great battles of this war.

40
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:10,310
One of the soldiers under his
command was Mauno Koivisto,

41
00:02:10,310 --> 00:02:13,590
who decades later became
President of Finland.

42
00:02:13,610 --> 00:02:18,470
In July 1944, Törni received
the Mannerheim Cross,

43
00:02:18,470 --> 00:02:21,540
Finland's highest
military decoration.

44
00:02:21,580 --> 00:02:25,910
In September 1944, Finland
concluded an armistice with

45
00:02:25,910 --> 00:02:27,440
the Soviet Union.

46
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:30,420
For Törni, the war was not over.

47
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:32,160
He joined a group

48
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:34,940
that wanted to resist a Soviet

49
00:02:34,940 --> 00:02:39,320
occupation, and in January
1945 he went to Germany

50
00:02:39,320 --> 00:02:42,420
to be trained as a saboteur.

51
00:02:42,450 --> 00:02:45,590
In the last weeks
of the war he fought

52
00:02:45,590 --> 00:02:51,680
in a Waffen-SS unit in northern Germany
and surrendered to British troops

53
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:52,930
in May 1945.

54
00:02:52,950 --> 00:02:56,430
He escaped from the prison
camp near Lübeck and made his

55
00:02:56,430 --> 00:02:58,200
way back to Finland.

56
00:02:58,220 --> 00:03:00,680
There the state
police arrested him.

57
00:03:00,710 --> 00:03:03,220
These images come from his file.

58
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:05,300
He was sentenced to six years in

59
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:06,940
prison for treason.

60
00:03:06,940 --> 00:03:09,260
Twice he escaped from prison,

61
00:03:09,260 --> 00:03:11,930
twice he was caught again.

62
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:17,820
In December 1948, President
Juho Paasikivi pardoned him.

63
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:21,020
But Törni no longer saw
a future in Finland.

64
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:25,520
In 1949 he went to Sweden and
signed on under a false name aboard

65
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:28,190
a ship bound for Venezuela.

66
00:03:28,210 --> 00:03:31,030
From there he sailed as
a seaman on a freighter

67
00:03:31,030 --> 00:03:32,780
heading for the USA.

68
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:36,290
In the Gulf of Mexico,
off the coast of Alabama,

69
00:03:36,290 --> 00:03:39,250
he jumped overboard
and swam ashore.

70
00:03:39,270 --> 00:03:42,240
A new law opened a path for him:

71
00:03:42,290 --> 00:03:45,260
the Lodge Act
allowed foreigners to

72
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:47,930
serve in the US Army and thereby

73
00:03:47,930 --> 00:03:49,980
gain citizenship.

74
00:03:50,010 --> 00:03:55,690
In 1954, Lauri Törni joined
the American army under the

75
00:03:55,690 --> 00:03:57,810
name Larry Thorne.

76
00:03:57,830 --> 00:04:01,510
He joined the Special Forces,
the Green Berets,

77
00:04:01,510 --> 00:04:04,710
became a citizen and
eventually an officer.

78
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:08,580
In 1962, operating
from Bad Tölz, he led a

79
00:04:08,580 --> 00:04:10,970
recovery mission in Iran.

80
00:04:10,990 --> 00:04:16,340
At an altitude of around 3,800 metres
in the Zagros Mountains, his team

81
00:04:16,340 --> 00:04:20,560
recovered the dead of a crashed US
aircraft and classified material,

82
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:24,480
after earlier search
parties had failed.

83
00:04:24,530 --> 00:04:29,040
From 1963, Thorne was
deployed in Vietnam.

84
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:33,540
In 1965 he belonged to a secret
unit tasked with bringing

85
00:04:33,540 --> 00:04:35,640
reconnaissance teams across

86
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:37,610
the border into Laos.

87
00:04:37,640 --> 00:04:43,030
On 18 October 1965 he took off
from Kham Duc in a helicopter

88
00:04:43,030 --> 00:04:46,540
of the South
Vietnamese Air Force.

89
00:04:46,570 --> 00:04:50,010
In bad weather the aircraft
crashed into a forested

90
00:04:50,010 --> 00:04:53,050
mountain area
southwest of Da Nang.

91
00:04:53,070 --> 00:04:55,310
The search was unsuccessful.

92
00:04:55,330 --> 00:04:58,150
Thorne was listed as
missing and was later

93
00:04:58,150 --> 00:04:59,890
promoted to major.

94
00:04:59,910 --> 00:05:05,480
Only in 1999 did an
American-Vietnamese team find the

95
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:08,460
crash site and his remains.

96
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:14,530
On 26 June 2003 he was buried
at Arlington National Cemetery,

97
00:05:14,530 --> 00:05:17,970
under the name Larry Thorne.

98
00:05:17,990 --> 00:05:21,750
Three uniforms,
two names and a life between

99
00:05:21,750 --> 00:05:23,150
the fronts.

100
00:05:23,170 --> 00:05:27,190
In Finland, many still regard
Lauri Törni as a war hero,

101
00:05:27,190 --> 00:05:29,980
while others point
to his service

102
00:05:29,980 --> 00:05:31,850
in the Waffen-SS.

103
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:33,260
His story shows how

104
00:05:33,260 --> 00:05:37,770
closely the fates of individual
people in the 20th century

105
00:05:37,770 --> 00:05:40,990
were bound up with
the great conflicts.

106
00:05:41,020 --> 00:05:43,260
How do you see Lauri Törni?

107
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:45,200
Write it in the comments.

